repository-code: "https://github.com/Urology-AI/digital-twin"
url: "https://urology-ai.github.io/digital-twin/"
abstract: >
  COMPASS is a preoperative decision-support platform that integrates clinical
  data with three imaging modalities (MRI, micro-ultrasound, PSMA PET/CT) plus
  optional Decipher genomic classifier results to predict surgical outcomes,
  side-specific nerve-sparing recommendations, and zone-level risk for patients
  undergoing robot-assisted radical prostatectomy. Developed and validated on a
  cohort of 5,352 consecutive patients with independent validation on 815
  trimodal imaging patients at Mount Sinai Health System.
keywords:
  - prostate cancer
  - radical prostatectomy
  - surgical planning
  - prediction model
  - PSMA PET
  - micro-ultrasound
  - MRI
  - digital twin
  - nerve sparing
